 {
   "id": "grammar.b2.24.04.perifrasis-andar-gerundio",
-  "title": "Perífrasis progresivas: Andar + gerundio",
+  "title": "Andar + Gerund",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "La perífrasis *andar + gerundio* denota una acción reiterada, dispersa, errática o sin un rumbo fijo, desarrollada en diversos momentos o lugares. Con frecuencia introduce un matiz de inquietud, reproche o informalidad coloquial en el discurso, sugiriendo que el sujeto se halla desasosegado o vagando en su tarea."
+      "content": "You know *estar* + gerund from A1 Unit 19, and in the last lesson you met *ir* + gerund. *Andar* + gerund also means that someone is doing something, but it adds the idea of going around: the action is spread over several days or places, and it has no clear direction. *Anda buscando trabajo* is \"He's going around looking for a job\". Speakers often add a note of worry or complaint, especially when they say it about someone else: *¿Por qué andas diciendo eso?* is \"Why are you going around saying that?\". *Andar* can be in any tense. Its preterite has an irregular stem: *anduve*, *anduvo*, *anduvimos*.",
+      "title": "Going around doing something"
     },
     {
       "type": "table",
-      "title": "Ejemplos de Andar + gerundio",
+      "title": "andar + gerund",
       "rows": [
         [
-          "El cronista anda buscando testimonios orales por los viejos bodegones de Boedo.",
-          "The chronicler is going around looking for oral testimonies in the old taverns of Boedo."
+          "Mi primo anda buscando casa por todas partes.",
+          "My cousin is going around looking for a house everywhere."
         ],
         [
-          "Andan diciendo en el barrio que la vieja librería va a transformarse en un centro cultural.",
-          "People around the neighborhood are going around saying that the old bookstore will become a cultural center."
+          "¿Por qué andas contando chismes de tus vecinos?",
+          "Why are you going around telling gossip about your neighbours?"
         ],
         [
-          "Silvio anda ideando inventos mecánicos en su humilde taller de Flores.",
-          "Silvio is going around devising mechanical inventions in his humble Flores workshop."
+          "Los vecinos andaban inquietos, preguntando por la obra.",
+          "The neighbours were going around uneasy, asking about the building work."
         ],
         [
-          "Los inspectores anduvieron revisando las condiciones de habitabilidad en los conventillos.",
-          "The inspectors went around inspecting the living conditions in the tenement houses."
+          "Anduvimos preguntando por el barrio, pero nadie sabía nada.",
+          "We went around the neighbourhood asking, but nobody knew anything."
         ]
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "No confundas *ir + gerundio* (proceso ordenado y paulatino hacia una meta) con *andar + gerundio* (proceso intermitente, desordenado, disperso o errático)."
+      "content": "Do not mix up *ir* and *andar* with a gerund. *Van arreglando la calle* means the street is being repaired bit by bit, in order. *Andan arreglando la calle* means the workers are around, doing repairs here and there, with no clear order. *Andar* + gerund is also very common in conversation, so it often sounds informal."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b2/b2-24-05-a-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b2/b2-24-05-a-gr.json
